_refine_special_details          
;
 H atoms were placed in idealised positions and refined using a riding
 model, with a common U restrained to be 1.2 (1.5 for methyl groups) times
 the equivalent isotropic displacement parameter of the parent atom.
 Methyl groups were treated as a rigid bodies and allowed to rotate about
 the E-CH3 bond but not tip. H atoms H3 and H5 were refined freely.
 The B alert in the check-cif file originating from the Hirshfeld test is
 probably a result of a minor positional disorder of silicon atom Si1 and
 carbon atom C18, which could not be modelled appropriately.


 Refinement of F^2^ against ALL reflections.  The weighted R-factor wR and
 goodness of fit S are based on F^2^, conventional R-factors R are based
 on F, with F set to zero for negative F^2^. The threshold expression of
 F^2^ > 2sigma(F^2^) is used only for calculating R-factors(gt) etc. and is
 not relevant to the choice of reflections for refinement.  R-factors based
 on F^2^ are statistically about twice as large as those based on F, and R-
 factors based on ALL data will be even larger.
;

